Description: Add Debian CEF library path to RPATH for ANGLE libraries
 CEF's default cmake config sets RPATH to "." (current directory), expecting
 applications to copy ANGLE libraries (libEGL.so, libGLESv2.so) next to the
 executable. However, Debian's FHS-compliant layout installs these to
 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef/ to avoid conflicts with system Mesa.
 .
 This causes CEF's GPU subprocess to load Mesa's libEGL.so instead of ANGLE's,
 because dlopen("libEGL.so.1") searches RPATH before ldconfig cache, and the
 executable's RPATH doesn't include Debian's CEF library path.
 .
 This patch adds /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef to the RPATH so that applications
 built with CEF cmake will automatically find the ANGLE libraries. This ensures
 the GPU subprocess loads the correct ANGLE implementation for hardware-accelerated
 rendering.
Author: Juan Manuel Mendez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-17

diff --git a/cef/cmake/cef_variables.cmake.in b/cef/cmake/cef_variables.cmake.in
index 1cd0c6e..c0ac38d 100644
--- a/cef/cmake/cef_variables.cmake.in
+++ b/cef/cmake/cef_variables.cmake.in
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ if(OS_LINUX)
     -pthread                        # Use the pthread library
     -Wl,--disable-new-dtags         # Don't generate new-style dynamic tags in ELF
     -Wl,--fatal-warnings            # Treat warnings as errors
-    -Wl,-rpath,.                    # Set rpath so that libraries can be placed next to the executable
+    -Wl,-rpath,.:/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef    # Set rpath for executable directory and Debian CEF library path
     -Wl,-z,noexecstack              # Mark the stack as non-executable (security feature)
     -Wl,-z,now                      # Resolve symbols on program start instead of on first use (security feature)
     -Wl,-z,relro                    # Mark relocation sections as read-only (security feature)
